From: Stephen Brennan <stephen.s.brennan@oracle.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 15:40:43 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] libbpf: Accept zero-filled BTF header extensions with swapped
 endianness

Pahole 1.32 emits a 32-byte BTF header even when the optional layout
section is disabled and both additional header fields are zero.
The libbpf bundled with Linux 5.10 through 7.0 rejects this header when
its endianness differs from the host, causing s390x kernel and external
module builds with a newer pahole to fail with:

  unsupported header length 32

Allow unknown header fields when they are all zero, since those bytes
need no byte swapping and can be preserved without interpreting them.
Validate the header length before checking the extension, and continue
to reject nonzero unknown fields.

This is a compatibility workaround for Linux 5.10 through 7.0. Linux 7.1
adds full layout header support in commit 087f3964f4b3 ("libbpf: Support
layout section handling in BTF").

Signed-off-by: Stephen Brennan <stephen.s.brennan@oracle.com>
---
 tools/lib/bpf/btf.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/lib/bpf/btf.c b/tools/lib/bpf/btf.c
index 83fe79ffcb8fb..a770495dca6ac 100644
--- a/tools/lib/bpf/btf.c
+++ b/tools/lib/bpf/btf.c
@@ -237,8 +237,20 @@ static int btf_parse_hdr(struct btf *btf)
 	}
 
 	if (hdr->magic == bswap_16(BTF_MAGIC)) {
+		__u32 hdr_len = bswap_32(hdr->hdr_len), i;
+
 		btf->swapped_endian = true;
-		if (bswap_32(hdr->hdr_len) != sizeof(struct btf_header)) {
+		if (hdr_len < sizeof(*hdr) || hdr_len > btf->raw_size) {
+			pr_debug("Invalid BTF header length %u\n", hdr_len);
+			return -EINVAL;
+		}
+		/*
+		 * Unknown header fields need no byte swapping if they are zero.
+		 * Reject non-zero extensions which we cannot interpret.
+		 */
+		for (i = sizeof(*hdr); i < hdr_len; i++) {
+			if (!((const char *)hdr)[i])
+				continue;
 			pr_warn("Can't load BTF with non-native endianness due to unsupported header length %u\n",
 				bswap_32(hdr->hdr_len));
 			return -ENOTSUP;
